@startuml sequence_health_stats
title Health and statistics: GET /api/health, GET /api/stats

actor Client
participant "ApiServer\n(GET /api/health,\nGET /api/stats)" as Api
participant OllamaClient
participant "ollama\n(container)" as Ollama
participant IndexService

== GET /api/health ==

Client -> Api : GET /api/health
activate Api
Api -> OllamaClient : isAvailable()
activate OllamaClient
note right of OllamaClient: checked on every call,\nno background polling

alt Ollama answers and lists the model
  OllamaClient -> Ollama : GET /api/tags (timeout 1 s)
  Ollama --> OllamaClient : 200 {"models": [{"name": "llama3.2:3b", ...}, ...]}
  OllamaClient --> Api : true
else Ollama answers, the model is not pulled yet
  OllamaClient -> Ollama : GET /api/tags (timeout 1 s)
  Ollama --> OllamaClient : 200, the model is not in "models"\n(or a non-200 status)
  OllamaClient --> Api : false
else Ollama too slow
  OllamaClient -> Ollama : GET /api/tags (timeout 1 s)
  Ollama -[#gray]-> OllamaClient : (no answer within 1 s)
  OllamaClient -> OllamaClient : catch HttpTimeoutException (IOException)
  OllamaClient --> Api : false
else Ollama unreachable
  OllamaClient -[#red]>x Ollama : GET /api/tags (connect timeout 1 s)
  OllamaClient -> OllamaClient : catch ConnectException (IOException)
  OllamaClient --> Api : false
end
deactivate OllamaClient
Api --> Client : 200 {"status": "ok", "ollama": true | false}
deactivate Api
note over Client, Api
  The backend does not depend on the model:
  the answer is 200 in every case, "ollama" says whether expansion can work.
end note

== GET /api/stats ==

Client -> Api : GET /api/stats
activate Api
Api -> IndexService : requireCurrent()
activate IndexService
IndexService -> IndexService : current.get()

alt an index is published
  IndexService --> Api : BuiltIndex(index, result, threads, docIds)
  Api --> Client : 200 {"documents": result.documentsIndexed(),\n"index_build_time_ms": result.timeMs(),\n"threads_used": threads}
else no index, building.get() is true
  note right of IndexService: rebuild() released the old\nindex with current.set(null)
  IndexService --> Api : throws ApiException(409, "index build in progress")
  Api --> Client : 409 {"status": "error",\n"message": "index build in progress"}
else no index, no build running
  IndexService --> Api : throws ApiException(409, "index has not been built yet")
  Api --> Client : 409 {"status": "error",\n"message": "index has not been built yet"}
end
deactivate IndexService
deactivate Api

@enduml
